load.t only asserts dynamic_libs returns a /vec/ path. It never proves the compiled extension actually loads into DBD::SQLite and creates a vec0 virtual table -- the real reason the dist exists. Add a functional smoke test (skip_all unless DBD::SQLite is available) that enables load_extension, loads the dynamic_libs path, and creates a vec0 table. Evidence: t/load.t lines 5-9.
